00:01:31.313 --> 00:01:36.773
Counterpoint Research's preliminary read of the third quarter of 2026 puts Mac shipments

00:01:36.773 --> 00:01:41.093
at 5.6 million units, down 11% from a year earlier.

00:01:41.693 --> 00:01:45.453
Worldwide PC shipments fell 21% to 57 million.

00:01:45.453 --> 00:01:52.773
and Apple's share rose from 8.7% to 9.8%. Apple remained the fourth largest vendor and

00:01:52.773 --> 00:01:58.033
counterpoint named the MacBook Neo as a key contributor to that result. Lenovo led at

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:10.353
26.3% with shipments down 23%. HP held 18.1% and fell 31%. Dell held 13.3% and fell 25%.

00:02:10.353 --> 00:02:18.033
ASUS in 5th fell 7% and held 9.2%, the only top 5 name with a smaller annual drop than Apple.

00:02:18.653 --> 00:02:24.073
Counterpoint expects global PC shipments to fall 27% year over year in the fourth quarter,

00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:27.933
and it sees 2027 broadly flat against 2026.

00:02:28.593 --> 00:02:32.033
Higher memory and component prices have fed through to PC prices,

00:02:32.453 --> 00:02:34.513
and consumers are postponing replacements.

