00:02:51.444 --> 00:02:57.704
pulled 8 co-pilot actions out of Windows 11 file explorer. CSIRO built serverless beacon

00:02:57.704 --> 00:03:03.564
called S beacon so genomic variant queries can run on Amazon web services without copying

00:03:03.564 --> 00:03:09.804
the data sets into a central database. Variant call files stay in Amazon S3 while disease

00:03:09.804 --> 00:03:13.384
These status, age, and location are indexed apart from those files.

00:03:14.004 --> 00:03:19.584
Onboarding builds Athena tables for that metadata, and ontology terms go through CSIRO's

00:03:19.584 --> 00:03:20.364
onto-server.

00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:26.724
A PI gateway routes a request to Lambda, and the variant module uses BCF tools and its

00:03:26.724 --> 00:03:32.044
HTS lib library to fetch only the needed slice through an HTTP byte-range request.

00:03:32.744 --> 00:03:36.864
Results come back through the Global Alliance for Genomics and Health Beacon API.

00:03:36.864 --> 00:03:44.784
InfoQ describes a test on chromosome 1 from the 1000 Genomes Project, 2500 4 samples in

00:03:44.784 --> 00:03:51.524
